/-!
# Genuine parameter differentiation under Haar Fourier integration

For the actual jointly smooth family on an open complex base times the
fixed unit torus, this package constructs its joint and base differentials
by descent through the original integer-lattice quotient. The base derivative
is a genuine jointly smooth family, not additional supplied data.

Local compactness and continuity of this actual differential supply a common
Haar-integrable bound. Full real Fréchet differentiation therefore commutes
with the genuine normalized Fourier coefficient. This proves native real
smoothness of each coefficient, and identifies arbitrary fixed-direction
iterated base derivatives with coefficients of actual derived families.
The preceding elliptic estimates give compact-uniform rapid decay and
summable polynomial majorants for these literal iterated derivatives.

All ambient representatives are used only on the original open base, with
no boundary regularity claim. No infinite-series synthesis or relative
cohomology/base-change assertion is made here.
-/
